{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Log","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exp_branchSum_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exp_branchSum_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.lean#L194-L237","doc":"**`exp (Σⱼ branchTerm x yⱼ) = 1` from Vieta alone.**\n\nStrictly weaker hypotheses than three copies of `exp_branchTerm_eq_one`: the\nsaddle condition is not used. The three products contribute\n\n    (∏ⱼ(−yⱼ))² / [ ∏ⱼ(1−yⱼ) · ∏ⱼ(1−x·yⱼ) · ∏ⱼ(1−yⱼ/x) ]\n      = 1 / ( 1 · x · (1/x) ) = 1\n\nwith `∏ⱼ(1−yⱼ) = 1` supplied by `prod_one_sub` above.\n\nThis is exactly the `hexp` hypothesis of\n`QOU.Archimedean.eq_zero_of_continuousOn_of_exp_eq_one`, so along the arc the\nsum of the deformed branch integers is pinned by its base-point value — given\ncontinuity, which is that lemma's remaining open input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.branch_data_of_curve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.branch_data_of_curve","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.lean#L177-L190","doc":"**The branch data of the deformed curve, derived.**\n\nEvery point of GGM's deformed 5₂ curve satisfies\n`2 log(−y) − log(1−y) − log(1−xy) − log(1−y/x) = k·(2πi)` for some integer `k`.\n\nThis is `branch_data_of_cubic` carried along the whole deformation. It comes\nfrom the curve alone: no dilogarithm, no analytic input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exp_branchTerm_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exp_branchTerm_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.lean#L160-L175","doc":"**`exp (branchTerm x y) = 1` on the curve.**\n\nThe exponential collapses the four logarithms to `y²/[(1−y)(1−xy)(1−y/x)]`,\nwhich the saddle condition makes `1`. No branch is chosen — that is the point,\nexactly as in `exp_branch_eq_one` at `x = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exp_branchTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exp_branchTerm","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.lean#L141-L158","doc":"**The exponential of `branchTerm`, evaluated.**\n\n`exp` collapses the four logarithms; clearing the `1/x` inside `1 − y/x` puts the\nresult over the cleared denominator `(1−y)(1−xy)(x−y)`, which is the shape the\nVieta products come in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.sub_ne_zero_of_one_sub_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.sub_ne_zero_of_one_sub_div","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.lean#L134-L139","doc":"`x − y ≠ 0` is the same condition as `1 − y/x ≠ 0`, off `x = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.branchTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.branchTerm","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.lean#L128-L132","doc":"The exponentiated `y·∂V/∂y`: the combination of logarithms that the saddle\ncondition sets to an integer multiple of `2πi`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.curve_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.curve_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.lean#L120-L122","doc":"…and at `x = 1` the curve is the 5₂ cubic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.saddle_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.saddle_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.lean#L114-L118","doc":"At `x = 1` this is the corpus's `y² = (1−y)³`\n(`FiveTwoSaddleSumRule.cubic_iff_sq_eq_cube`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.deformed_saddle_iff_curve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.deformed_saddle_iff_curve","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.lean#L104-L112","doc":"**The deformed saddle condition is identically the curve.**\n\n`x·y² = (1−y)(1−x·y)(x−y)` is `y² = (1−y)(1−xy)(1−y/x)` with the `1/x` cleared,\ni.e. `∂V/∂y = 0` after exponentiating. It holds exactly on the curve — over any\ncommutative ring, with no positivity, ordering, or analysis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.curve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.curve","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.lean#L101-L102","doc":"GGM's deformed 5₂ curve. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.prod_one_sub'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.prod_one_sub'","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.lean#L91-L97","doc":"The field form of `prod_one_sub`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.prod_one_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.prod_one_sub","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.lean#L78-L89","doc":"**`∏ⱼ (1 − yⱼ) = 1`**, in cleared form.\n\nHypotheses are Vieta for `x·y³ − (x²+1)·y² + (x²+x+1)·y − x = 0`, matching\n`prod_one_sub_x_mul` and `prod_x_sub` in `FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch`. The cleared\nstatement `x·∏ = x` is what survives over a general `CommRing`; divide by `x` in\na field. ","signatureChunk":0}]}